  "description": "<p>Migrating a single object from 400,000 objects takes approximately 3.5 hours in our environment, despite using a pre-generated datastream index.  Upon examination, it looks like every single object is scanned (from the filesystem?) then checked to see if it should be migrated.</p>\n\n<p>I ran the following command at 10:02 AM:</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\njava -jar target/migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar --source-type=akubra --datastreams-dir=/fedora3-prod/fedora/datastreams --objects-dir=/fedora3-prod/fedora/objects --target-dir=/fedora-migration-test --layout=pairtree --pid-file=/<span class=\"code-keyword\">var</span>/tmp/test-migration-pids.txt --index-dir=/<span class=\"code-keyword\">var</span>/tmp/datastream-index --debug</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>The file <tt>/var/tmp/test-migration-pids.txt</tt> contains a PID for a single object.</p>\n\n<p>Looking at the debug log, I saw many of these entries, one per object in our repository:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nDEBUG 10:02:16.741 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:2IWVGDIWTE4FU8Q, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>\r\n DEBUG 10:02:16.765 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:X6FSD5T4JBUPS9D, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>\r\n DEBUG 10:02:16.786 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:56KTJDLD47H2D8R, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>\r\n DEBUG 10:02:16.816 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:6OKBI5VJH3DD49B, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>\r\n DEBUG 10:02:16.840 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:ALJVKGFZONRTD8R, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>\r\n DEBUG 10:02:16.863 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:5U7C22BGOOC6C8B, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span></pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Migration-utils scanned approximately 25 - 30 object per second.  There are 390,925 objects in our repository.</p>\n\n<p>At 10:35, it found the object to migrate, and migrated it:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nDEBUG 10:35:38.890 (UserProvidedPidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:4RJO2AJNM55JH82, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">true</span>\r\nDEBUG 10:35:38.910 (ResumePidListManager) PID: 1711.dl:4RJO2AJNM55JH82, accept? <span class=\"code-keyword\">true</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>After migrating it, it migration-utils then continued to scan through the rest of the objects in our repository.  It finished running at 1:28 PM.<br/>\n Total run time for one object:  3 hours 26 minutes.</p>\n\n<p>Recommendations for partial migrations, reading from a PID list:</p>\n\n<p>1.  Stop the migration when the last PID in the list is migrated.</p>\n\n<p>2.  Generate a reusable object index, similar to the datastream index, that can be quickly scanned on subsequent runs.</p>",
